      "properties": {},
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653",
      "widgets_values": [
        "## How to test the Krea 2 Prompt Writer\n\n1. **Write new prompt**: type your idea in `brief`, press **Run**. The language model on .159 writes the prompt (about 15\u201340 s), then the image renders.\n2. After the run the prompt appears in `current_prompt` and the mode switches to **Keep current prompt**. Run again = same prompt, same image.\n3. **Apply change**: set the mode, type e.g. `make the bikini red, camera lower` in `change`, press **Run**. Only that part of the prompt changes; `change` is cleared afterwards.\n4. You can also edit `current_prompt` by hand and run in Keep mode.\n\nThe seed is fixed, so each image shows only the effect of your change. Set the seed to -1 for a new random seed each run.\n\n`aspect_ratio` **Auto** uses the ratio the writer picks (vertical for UGC/selfies). Nude, topless and sex briefs work; for *partial* nudity (topless with shorts) switch **Enable LoRA?** off, the LoRA tends to undress fully.\n"
      ]
    }
